## Business Rules-Wallet

| **ID** | **Business Rule** |
| --- | --- |
| **BR-W01** | Recharge codes must contain exactly 14 digits. |
| **BR-W02** | Only valid, active, unused codes can be redeemed. |
| **BR-W03** | A recharge code can be redeemed only once. |
| **BR-W04** | Each successful redemption credits the corresponding code value to the student's wallet. |
| **BR-W05** | Five consecutive failed redemption attempts trigger a 15-minute top-up lock. |
| **BR-W06** | Failed attempts include nonexistent, already-used, expired, or otherwise invalid codes. |
| **BR-W07** | Successful redemption resets the failed-attempt counter to zero. |
| **BR-W08** | A locked user cannot redeem codes until the 15-minute lock expires (expiration automatically resets the counter). |
| **BR-W09** | A successful redemption must update the code status, wallet balance, and transaction record consistently within a single atomic transaction. |
| **BR-W10** | The system must prevent simultaneous redemption of the same code using database row locks or conditional updates (Concurrency Control). |

