## Business Rules - Class Purchase & Playback

| **ID** | **Business Rule** |
| --- | --- |
| **BR-CP01** | A student cannot purchase an unpublished, disabled, or unavailable class. |
| **BR-CP02** | An actively enrolled student cannot purchase the same class again. |
| **BR-CP03** | A student must have sufficient wallet balance to purchase a class. |
| **BR-CP04** | The system must re-verify the balance inside an atomic transaction before deducting to prevent simultaneous double-spending (Race Conditions). |
| **BR-CP05** | Successful purchase deducts the price, creates a wallet transaction record, and creates an enrollment record atomically. |
| **BR-CP06** | Only students with an "Active" enrollment status can access protected class content (suspended or refunded enrollments are blocked). |
| **BR-CP07** | Video playback requires a short-lived playback authorization token from the DRM provider for every session. |
| **BR-CP08** | Video content must be delivered exclusively through the approved encrypted DRM mechanism; direct MP4 URLs are strictly prohibited. |
| **BR-CP09** | Video playback must include a dynamic watermark displaying the student's masked phone number (e.g., 010****1234) to protect privacy while deterring piracy. |
| **BR-CP10** | Attached PDFs and homework links must enforce their own entitlement checks independently from the video player. |

