## **2. Business Rules (Administrative Operations)**

| **ID** | **Business Rule** |
| --- | --- |
| **BR-AD01** | Administrative operations must require authenticated access with valid session tokens. |
| **BR-AD02** | Each administrative role (Super Admin vs. Assistant) must have explicitly defined permissions (RBAC) enforced by the backend, not just by hiding UI buttons. |
| **BR-AD03** | Scratch codes must be cryptographically generated and checked for database-level uniqueness to prevent collisions. |
| **BR-AD04** | Each code must be securely stored (e.g., using a secure hash for validation) and associated with a specific batch ID and monetary value. |
| **BR-AD05** | Raw recharge codes must be protected against unauthorized access and should ideally be exportable only once upon generation. |
| **BR-AD06** | A class cannot be published; it must remain in a "Processing" or "Ready/Draft" state until the DRM provider successfully completes video encryption. |
| **BR-AD07** | Student information displayed in the support dashboard must be masked (e.g., partial phone numbers/codes) according to the operator's permission level (Principle of Least Privilege). |
| **BR-AD08** | Resetting a student's devices must explicitly revoke all active authentication sessions (Log out from all devices) in addition to clearing the allowed devices array. |
| **BR-AD09** | Changing a student's primary phone number requires strict identity verification (e.g., OTP sent to the parent) and must invalidate existing sessions to prevent account hijacking. |
| **BR-AD10** | Every sensitive administrative action (generating codes, publishing classes, resetting devices, changing numbers) must be permanently recorded in an append-only Audit Log containing the Operator ID and timestamp. |
